Architecture plan for issues #71-#79

Context
- Product: chen-hatti-f810-dailypapers, a Next.js 16 App Router dashboard for daily research papers and GitHub repositories.
- Persistence remains PostgreSQL via Prisma. Existing Item/Paper/Repository/Summary/Tag/Note models are sufficient for this delta; new source-specific metadata should live in existing JSON/string array fields unless a later issue explicitly requires schema changes.
- Existing layering should be preserved: fetchers in src/fetchers, business services in src/services, validation schemas in src/validators, route handlers in src/app/api, UI components in src/components, tests in tests.

Module structure and file organization
1. Hugging Face Daily Papers fetcher (#71)
   - Add src/fetchers/huggingface.ts and export it from src/fetchers/index.ts.
   - Define types such as HuggingFaceDailyPaperMetadata with title, authors, abstract/summary, sourceUrl, canonicalUrl, arxivId, hfLikes, hfRank, publishedAt, pdfUrl/landingUrl where available.
   - Reuse arXiv helpers from src/fetchers/arxiv.ts for ID extraction/canonical URL normalization. If HF entries include arXiv links, resolve those to existing arXiv metadata when practical.
   - Add src/validators/huggingface.ts for maxResults and fetch input parsing.

2. Hugging Face daily-fetch service (#72)
   - Add src/services/huggingface-daily-fetch.ts.
   - Fetch/sort top HF daily papers by attention, default top 5, cap with HUGGINGFACE_DAILY_PAPERS_MAX_RESULTS.
   - Persist using existing Item + Paper shape. Put source metadata in paper.analysis, e.g. { source: "huggingface-daily", hfLikes, hfRank, huggingFaceUrl, resolvedArxivId }.
   - Deduplicate by canonicalUrl/arXiv ID before create. Support dryRun and autoSummarize by reusing summarizePaper.

3. GitHub fastest-growing service (#73)
   - Add src/services/github-fastest-growing-fetch.ts.
   - Reuse src/fetchers/github.ts searchGitHubTrendingRepositories/request path. Approximate momentum via created/pushed lookback + stars sort.
   - Persist/update Repository items using existing Item + Repository shape. No schema change.
   - Configurable env/defaults: GITHUB_FAST_GROWING_MAX_RESULTS, GITHUB_FAST_GROWING_LOOKBACK_DAYS, GITHUB_FAST_GROWING_CANDIDATE_LIMIT.
   - Support dryRun and optional autoSummarize.

4. Unified daily-fetch API (#74)
   - Add src/app/api/daily-fetch/route.ts.
   - Accept GET query params and POST JSON body, using a new validator schema in src/validators/daily-fetch.ts.
   - Run HF Top-5 paper service + GitHub fastest-growing Top-5 service and return { papers, repositories } with per-source fetched/ingested/skipped/failed status details.
   - Keep existing /api/arxiv/daily-fetch and /api/github/trending-fetch endpoints unchanged for backward compatibility.

5. Env vars and README (#75)
   - Update .env.example and README.md with the new HF and fastest-growing GitHub settings.
   - Clarify that GITHUB_TOKEN remains required for GitHub API calls.
   - Describe /api/daily-fetch as the preferred combined daily source while documenting legacy endpoints.

6. arXiv topic/field presets (#76)
   - Add src/services/arxiv-topic-presets.ts or src/config/arxiv-topic-presets.ts.
   - Shared FieldPreset type: id, labelEn, labelZh, keywords, description.
   - Presets: LLM/Agents, Computer Vision, Robotics, NLP, Systems, Custom.
   - Keep this independent of fetch logic so UI and service tests can consume the same mapping.

7. Dashboard field switcher (#77)
   - Extend src/components/dashboard-control-bar.tsx control state with selected field preset.
   - Update filtering in src/components/home-content.tsx to match preset keywords against paper tags/topics/abstract/summary/relevance notes where available.
   - Label the UI "Latest Top Papers by Field".
   - Avoid breaking existing query/type/date/topic/relevance/sort controls.

8. arXiv latest-papers fetch panel (#78)
   - Add/extend a dashboard panel component, likely near AddItemPanel, for field preset, maxResults, autoSummarize and POST /api/arxiv/daily-fetch.
   - Send preset keywords from shared topic config. Show fetched/ingested/skipped/failed counts and refresh the dashboard on success.
   - Keep failure states explicit and user-readable.

9. Tests (#79)
   - Extend tests/fetchers.test.ts for HF parsing, sorting by likes/upvotes, and arXiv ID resolution.
   - Add service tests for GitHub fastest-growing candidate selection and persistence/dryRun behavior using mocked fetch.
   - Add tests for topic preset keyword mapping and fetch-panel payload construction/filter state where feasible.
   - Keep existing node --import tsx --test test runner.

Dependencies between issues
- #71 is prerequisite for #72.
- #72 and #73 are prerequisites for #74.
- #74 is prerequisite for #75 docs/API examples.
- #76 is prerequisite for #77 and #78.
- #79 depends on all implementation issues.

Key design decisions
- Do not add new database tables for HF/GitHub ranking metadata; use Paper.analysis JSON and existing Repository fields to honor "No schema change" where stated.
- Keep fetchers pure and easily mockable: external HTTP parsing belongs in fetchers; persistence belongs in services.
- Preserve existing canonical/dedup rules by normalizing arXiv IDs and GitHub repository URLs before writes.
- Combined daily-fetch should aggregate per-source errors instead of failing the whole request when one source fails.
- UI additions should reuse existing language/theme/control patterns and avoid auth or object-storage assumptions.
